  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "registration-table",
      "claim": "Core-served provider types are one entry each in a per-type registration table (openai_codex, google_antigravity, opencode_zen), each in its own file; the Runtime's single credential store dispatches by instance type, and Codex and Antigravity behave as before.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/core_runtime.go, codex_vertical.go, antigravity_vertical.go, zen_vertical.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "zen-through-runtime",
      "claim": "OpenCode Zen Chat, Responses and both streams go through the llmgw-core Runtime with core's Zen vertical. Credentials resolve with connection precedence (personal connection, system connection, configured key); when none resolves the request is sent anonymously, as before. The gateway's Zen branches in OpenAIProvider and bearerAuth and its Zen stream assembly are removed; instruction sanitizing, event re-encoding, the adapted header and the Chat fallback on a Responses 404 or 405 stay in the gateway, and client-visible stream data is unchanged.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/zen_vertical.go, opencode_zen.go, openai.go; go/internal/api/testdata unchanged"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "deviations",
      "claim": "Edge-case differences: error messages come from core and no longer quote upstream bodies; an HTTP-date Retry-After reaches the client as seconds; credentials are resolved per request, so a revoked connection is never used; a stream that breaks while an anonymous completion is assembled is retried or failed over per core's classification. None affects a successful request, the CLI, health or the public models list.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/zen_vertical.go and Zen tests"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "suite",
      "claim": "The full Go suite passes with HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY unreachable with unchanged characterization goldens and coupling budgets; gofmt, vet, govulncheck (0 reachable), check-docs and git diff --check pass.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "local gate run on the reviewed head"
      }
    }
  ],
